				"paragraphs": ["Useful views can include the pair together, both sides, heels, soles, size labels and a close-up of a specific concern. Choose views to resolve your uncertainty rather than requesting a large photo set without a purpose. For a measurement, ask for the start and end points to be visible with the ruler in the same plane where possible. A tilted ruler or cropped zero point can make a number hard to interpret.", "Photographs can support observations about visible condition and measurements shown in the frame. They cannot establish long-term sole adhesion, cushioning durability, waterproof performance, material chemistry or authenticity. If the purchase depends on one of those properties, look for appropriate evidence beyond ordinary warehouse photos. A clean-looking image is not a laboratory test or a brand-authorised authentication result."]
