				"paragraphs": ["Write down which observations matter enough to change your decision. A wrong size label, a missing lace or a visible tear needs a different response from uncertainty about a colour under artificial light. Make your request factual: identify the item, describe the visible issue and specify the additional image or action you need. Save the original listing and current photos together so the comparison remains understandable later.", "Resolve important uncertainties before approving international shipment when the platform allows that choice. Confirm the actual return or exchange conditions for your order rather than assuming all sellers offer the same window. Do not treat this guide as a promise of a free return, a particular inspection service or compensation. Those decisions depend on the seller, service and live terms associated with the purchase."]
